g Me the Horizon", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "at", "country_name": "Austria", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": 37306, "best_position": 6}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": 26578, "best_position": 54}, {"artist": "Tove Lo", "streams": 26185, "best_position": 7}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": 24902, "best_position": 9}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": 12131, "best_position": 21}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": 8567, "best_position": 73}, {"artist": "David Guetta", "streams": 8108, "best_position": 86}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chappell Roan", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "folk": {"genre": "folk", "country_code": "at", "country_name": "Austria", "summary": "Folk music can have a number of different meanings, including:\n\nTraditional music: The original meaning of the term \"folk music\" was synonymous with the term \"Traditional music\", also often including Roots music; the term \"Traditional music\" was given its more specific meaning to distinguish it from the other definitions that \"Folk music\" is now considered to encompass.\nFolk music can also describe a particular kind of popular music which is based on traditional music.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Olivia Rodrigo", "streams": 32278, "best_position": 18}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": 8567, "best_position": 73}, {"artist": "Alex G", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Clairo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ellie Goulding", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lorde", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Phoebe Bridgers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "at", "country_name": "Austria", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": 26578, "best_position": 54}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 18735, "best_position": 44}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 14735, "best_position": 12}, {"artist": "Mac Miller", "streams": 8862, "best_position": 65}, {"artist": "Black Eyed Peas", "streams": 7882, "best_position": 93}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": 7875, "best_position": 95}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "metal": {"genre": "metal", "country_code": "at", "country_name": "Austria", "summary": "A metal is a material that exhibits a lustrous appearance when polished or fractured and conducts electricity and heat relatively efficiently. These properties are associated with the presence of electrons at the Fermi level. Metals are typically ductile, allowing them to be drawn into wires, and malleable, enabling them to be shaped by hammering or pressing.\n\nA metal may be a chemical element, such as iron, an alloy such as stainless steel, or a molecular compound such as polymeric sulfur nitride.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": 28577, "best_position": 48}, {"artist": "Evanescence", "streams": 8063, "best_position": 88}, {"artist": "Bring Me the Horizon", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Limp Bizkit", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Metallica", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Nirvana", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Red Hot Chili Peppers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Slipknot", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "System of a Down", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "new wave": {"genre": "new wave", "country_code": "at", "country_name": "Austria", "summary": "New wave is today a quite broad umbrella term describing popular music from around 1977 to 1986. But originally it was a slim sub genre of Western popular music that arose in the United Kingdom about 1977-78. It had close ties to punk rock and fairly strong influences of the musical style that had been invented and continuously developed throughout the 1970s: reggae.\n\nThe term new wave was first a kind of description of a more musical and lyric wise complex music than punk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "The Killers", "streams": 23355, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "David Bowie", "s